course: dictionary
lesson: 6083
title: Metamorphic rock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about science, and science words often have a clear, exact meaning. «Metamorphic rocks are rocks changed by heat and pressure without melting.» The important clue is the phrase without melting. The rock changes shape and hardness, but it never turns into liquid.
explain: Look at the word parts and the words around it. Meta- can mean change, and morph means form or shape, so metamorphic means changed in form. Outside science, you can use it the same way: a caterpillar going through a metamorphosis is a big change of form.
explain: Scientists sort all rocks into three families. «All rocks belong to three families: igneous, sedimentary and metamorphic.» To find the right family, ask how the rock was made: by melting and cooling, by layers pressed together, or by heat and pressure changing it.
fact: Metamorphic means changed by heat and pressure, without melting.
fact: The three rock families are igneous, sedimentary and metamorphic.
fact: «Limestone becomes marble» and «shale becomes slate»: both are examples of metamorphic rock.
fact: In the rock cycle, rocks can change from one family into another over millions of years.
fact: Metamorphic also means to do with a big change of form, so it can describe any great change in shape.
exercise: «Metamorphic rocks are rocks changed by heat and pressure without melting.» What does metamorphic rock mean? | *Rock changed by heat and pressure without melting | Rock that has melted and cooled | Rock that is soft and wet | Rock made of tiny bits pressed together
exercise: Limestone can change into marble. Which rock family does marble belong to? | Sedimentary | Igneous | *Metamorphic
exercise: «In the rock cycle, rocks are worn down into bits that make sedimentary rock.» Shale can change into slate. Which kind of rock is slate? | Igneous | *Metamorphic | Sedimentary
test: Which change makes a rock metamorphic? | Being worn down into small bits | Being left out in the rain | *Heat and pressure, without melting | Melting and cooling into liquid rock
test: Which change shows a metamorphic rock being made? | *Limestone changing into marble | Rock worn down into small bits that settle in layers | Melted rock cooling into a hard rock
exam: «The rock cycle» describes how rocks change over time. Which process makes a metamorphic rock? | Melting and cooling | *Heat and pressure, without melting | Being left out in the rain | Being worn down into bits
